    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/CommunicationThreadReadService.cs</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/CommunicationThreadReadModels.cs</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/CommunicationEndpoints.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/integration/seam/Communication/*.cs</output>
  </outputs>
  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a caller who can see a record-less (Direct) thread T, when `GET /api/communications/threads` is called, then T appears in the list.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a caller, when the list returns, then it equals the set the impersonated `sprk_communicationthreads` query returns for that caller (access parity) — no post-hoc regarding scoping.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a thread P the caller has NO access to, when the caller lists threads, then P is absent (negative-access; no over-disclosure) and no membership-union was computed.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given `?search=acme`, when the list returns, then only threads whose `sprk_name` matches "acme" are returned (name search), with the value safely escaped.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given more threads than the page size, when paging through with the returned token/index, then pages are stable and non-overlapping under a deterministic order.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given an unresolved caller, when the endpoint is called, then it returns 403 (fail-closed, no app-only fallback).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the new read method, when its dependencies are inspected, then it takes no membership-resolution/`IThreadPrivateGrantProvider` dependency (structural no-union guard, seam test).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the new `GET /threads` route, when the app starts, then it does not collide with `/threads/{threadId}/messages` or `POST /threads/direct` (routing resolves unambiguously).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">BFF publish measured ≤60 MB compressed; delta reported in task notes/PR (per .claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">All tests pass; 0 new HIGH CVE (dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive).</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>
  <notes>Placement Justification MUST be stated in the PR (cite .claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md): new endpoint + method inside `Services/Communication/`, reusing the impersonation + shared-filter pipeline; no new package/AI/worker; publish delta ≈0. Reference spec FR-16 + Success Criterion 5. Run `/conflict-check` before opening the PR (shared `Services/Communication/**`).</notes>
